[hr]

[size=14pt][b]Claude's explanation[/b][/size]

[list]
[li][b]The Threat War Effort[/b] - a permanent intel screen ranking every infested system by urgency: vitality, garrisons, reach, strikes out, sieges in, production, Purge and mission buttons.[/li]
[li]Systems you have not found are listed as [i]Unknown[/i] - figures shown, location hidden.[/li]
[li]Per-world cards with a [i]Colony[/i] button that opens vanilla's own colony screen.[/li]
[li]The Threat founds real colonies that mine, refine, forge and grow in a closed hive economy that builds every fleet they field.[/li]
[li]That economy is vanilla's: each world draws from its single best source, so one producer feeds the whole hive - the hive builds spare refineries, forges and fuel plants across systems, and cutting a resource means cutting every copy.[/li]
[li]The home system carries Domain relics (Pristine Nanoforge, Mantle Bore, Synchrotron, ...) that feed the entire network - the hub worth taking, and the loot for taking it.[/li]
[li]Hive ports are Spaceports; a disrupted port cuts the world's shipping to a trickle and starves it.[/li]
[li]Every input counts in Hive Vitality, rare ore and rare metals included.[/li]
[li]Reach is fuel and fleets for everyone: 4 ly per unit of fuel a colony's fleets can carry, hive and factions alike. Cut the hive's fuel and the swarm stops.[/li]
[li]Hive worlds run three organs: Fabrication Core (growth, machinery), Swarm Nexus (Defense Swarms, expeditions), marine-free defenses fed on metals and machinery.[/li]
[li]Expeditions are mustered from a colony's own Defense Swarms - kill its swarms and you have grounded it; a fleet still fabricating in orbit can be stopped at the staging colony.[/li]
[li]Worlds the swarm destroys, it colonizes.[/li]
[li]Colonies die only through decline: suppress or starve the organs below 35% vitality until the population collapses. No bombardment reduces population.[/li]
[li]Disrupted defenses and organs wear down with the disruption days on their clock - repeated raids lower the defense figure, the raid odds and the bombardment bill.[/li]
[li]NPC purges and commissioned expeditions are sized to the target's defenses; the commission quote shows the landing force against what a raid needs before you pay.[/li]
[li]Raids land on whatever hurts the hive most on that world - Core, Nexus, an importing port, or the hive's best source of a resource.[/li]
[li]After-action sitreps arrive the moment operations end, every blow dated.[/li]
[li]Defense-board contracts are ordinary missions from phase 3: immediate and strategic tiers, accept or ignore, a clock once taken.[/li]
[li]Every economy, reach, siege and decline number is configurable via LunaLib (Shift+F2) or [tt]data/config/settings.json[/tt].[/li]
[li]For Starsector 0.98a-RC8. Vanilla-only, LunaLib optional. Safe to add to an existing save; removing it mid-incursion breaks the save.[/li]
[/list]

